{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778552436,"nonce":"f9ojBj+3x0i7gFkpIhjxdFnhQpg=","title":"Use conversation ID for auth event delivery persistence across session restarts","message":"When Claude Code restarts (resume/continue), the channel server gets a new `MANDIBLE_SESSION_ID`. Auth requests submitted under the old session ID no longer match for channel-event delivery, and the startup catch-up query also misses them since it queries by the new session ID.\n\n**Available identifier:** `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` (env var set by Claude Code) persists across resumes — it is the conversation/chat ID, not the ephemeral process session ID. Confirmed via `env | grep CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` across restarts.\n\n**Design:**\n\n1. Channel server startup: read `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` from env, send it alongside `MANDIBLE_SESSION_ID` during session registration (`POST /api/sessions/register`).\n2. Mandible stores the mapping in the `sessions` table: add a `conversation_id` column.\n3. `mandible auth request` CLI: also send `conversation_id` (read from `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`) alongside `target_session_id` in the POST body. Store on the auth_request row.\n4. Auth event delivery (`buildResolvedPayload`): include `conversation_id` in the SSE payload so the channel server can match by conversation ID when session IDs differ.\n5. Channel server `dispatchEvent`: match on `target_session_id` OR `target_conversation_id` (when target_session_id does not match but conversation_id does, treat as owner match).\n6. Startup catch-up (`runStartupCatchUp`): query undelivered auth results by conversation_id in addition to session_id.\n\nThis ensures a resumed session inherits its predecessor's pending auth requests without manual intervention.\n\nSurfaced during testing: auth request `6b662cf1` had `target_session_id` matching the pre-restart session but the post-restart session never received the channel event.","files":null}]}